4) READ REPAIR — SELF HEALING DURING READS
================================================================================

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
INTUITION
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

When a read detects stale replica,
system repairs it immediately.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FLOW
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Client reads:
A = 120
C = 100

Latest chosen:
120

Now system writes:
C ← 120

Now:
A = 120
B = 120
C = 120

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
REAL LIFE ANALOGY
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Suppose 3 teammates maintain same spreadsheet.

One teammate old version de raha hai.
Meeting ke time updated sheet share karke uski copy bhi fix kar di.

This is read repair.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WHY IMPORTANT
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

- stale replicas heal automatically
- hot keys quickly converge
- no manual recovery needed

Tradeoff:
slightly slower reads.

================================================================================
5) LIMITATION OF READ REPAIR
================================================================================

Important FAANG point:

Read repair only fixes:
DATA THAT GETS READ

Cold keys may remain stale forever.

Example:
Old product SKU never queried.
That stale replica never heals.

So we need:
BACKGROUND REPAIR

This is:
ANTI-ENTROPY

================================================================================
6) ANTI-ENTROPY — BACKGROUND RECONCILIATION
================================================================================

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
INTUITION
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Replicas periodically compare data in background.

No client request needed.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
REAL LIFE EXAMPLE
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Every night all branch offices compare salary sheets.

Differences sync ho jaate hain.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WHY CALLED ANTI-ENTROPY?
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Entropy = disorder / divergence
Anti-entropy = restoring order

Goal:
all replicas converge eventually.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
IMPORTANT JORDAN LINE (VERY DEEP)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

"We only want to send writes that are missing.
We do NOT want to send full replication log."

WHY?

Because full log:
- too large
- too much network bandwidth
- too many unnecessary writes
- expensive for millions of keys

So big question:

How do we quickly know
WHICH writes are different?

================================================================================
7) THE CORE PROBLEM — QUICK DIFFERENCE DETECTION
================================================================================

Naive way:
compare full database row by row ❌

For huge systems:
- billions of keys
- petabytes of data

Impossible.

Need:
FAST way to locate changed ranges only.

This is where:
MERKLE TREE enters.

================================================================================
8) MERKLE TREE — THE GENIUS IDEA
================================================================================

Merkle Tree = Hash Tree

Instead of comparing raw data,
compare HASHES of chunks.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
REAL LIFE ANALOGY
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

2 companies want to compare financial books.

Instead of checking every invoice:
first compare department summaries.

If summary same:
skip entire department.

If mismatch:
drill deeper.

This saves huge work.

================================================================================
9) MERKLE TREE STRUCTURE
================================================================================

Example data blocks:
[10, 20, 30, 40]

Leaf hashes:
h1 = H(10)
h2 = H(20)
h3 = H(30)
h4 = H(40)

Upper layer:
h12 = H(h1 + h2)
h34 = H(h3 + h4)

Root:
hroot = H(h12 + h34)

So root represents:
ENTIRE DATASET SUMMARY

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
VISUAL DIAGRAM
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

                Root
              /      \
           h12        h34
          /  \       /   \
        h1   h2    h3    h4
       10   20    30    40

================================================================================
10) HOW IT ANSWERS: "WHICH WRITES TO SEND?"
================================================================================

This is the most important interview insight.

Instead of sending:
full replication log ❌

We compare:
Merkle roots ✅

If roots same:
no writes needed

If roots differ:
go one level deeper

Only mismatched subtree explored.

This quickly narrows exact changed data.

================================================================================
11) TWO TREE EXAMPLE — 2 COMPANIES DATA COMPARISON
================================================================================

Company A values:
[10, 20, 30, 40]

Company B values:
[10, 25, 30, 40]

Only one value changed.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
STEP 1: ROOT CHECK
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

rootA ≠ rootB
→ some mismatch exists

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
STEP 2: LEFT vs RIGHT SUBTREE
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Right subtree:
[30,40] same ✅

Left subtree:
[10,20] vs [10,25] mismatch ❌

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
STEP 3: GO DEEPER
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Compare:
10 vs 10 → same
20 vs 25 → mismatch found

Now only sync:
20 ↔ 25

This is why Merkle trees are insanely efficient.

================================================================================
12) TIME COMPLEXITY INTUITION
================================================================================

Without Merkle:
O(N) full compare

With Merkle:
O(log N) to locate mismatch path
+ only changed chunk transfer

Massive bandwidth savings.

